          "quantity": 75,
          "unit": "ml",
          "category": "despensa"
        },
        {
          "name": "Soy sauce",
          "quantity": 2,
          "unit": "tablespoons",
          "category": "condimentos"
        },
        {
          "name": "Rice vinegar",
          "quantity": 2,
          "unit": "tablespoons",
          "category": "granos"
        },
        {
          "name": "Sesame seed",
          "quantity": 0.5,
          "unit": "tbs",
          "category": "otros"
        },
        {
          "name": "Spring onions",
          "quantity": 2,
          "unit": "sliced",
          "category": "verduras"
        }
      ],
      "steps": [
        {
          "text": "step 1"
        },
        {
          "text": "Tip the cabbage into a food processor and blitz until finely chopped"
        },
        {
          "text": "Season with ½ tsp salt, toss well and set aside for 15 mins"
        },
        {
          "text": "Tip into a clean tea towel and squeeze out as much water as you can"
        },
        {
          "text": "Tip into a bowl with the carrot, mushrooms, pork mince, garlic, ginger, soy sauce, sesame oil and spring onions"
        },
        {
          "text": "Season with black pepper"
        },
        {
          "text": "Scrunch everything together using your hands, mixing well until everything is combined"
        },
        {
          "text": "step 2"
        },
        {
          "text": "Soak the spring roll sheets for a couple of seconds in a shallow dish of warm water, then transfer to an oiled chopping board"
        },
        {
          "text": "Working with one sheet at a time, spoon 1 heaped tbsp of the filling into the middle, then fold the bottom up and over the filling"
        },
        {
          "text": "Fold down the top of the sheet, then the sides to fully encase and make a neat square"
        },
        {
          "text": "If the dumpling feels a little fragile, soak another sheet and wrap it again"
        },
        {
          "text": "Repeat with the remaining sheets and filling, transferring the dumplings to an oiled plate as you go"
        },
        {
          "text": "step 3"
        },
        {
          "text": "Heat the oil in a large, non-stick frying pan (ensuring it is no more than a third full) over a medium-high heat and fry the dumplings for 3-5 mins until golden brown"
        },
        {
          "text": "Use a slotted spoon or spider to turn them, then cover with a lid and cook for another 3-4 mins until golden"
        },
        {
          "text": "Remove the lid and cook for 1-2 mins"
        },
        {
          "text": "step 4"
        },
        {
          "text": "Meanwhile, combine all the dipping sauce ingredients in small bowl"
        },
        {
          "text": "Serve the dumplings with the dipping sauce on the side."
        }
      ],
