    {
      "id": "tmdb-53448",
      "title": "Tendir Choreyi (Tandoori Bread)",
      "description": "Receta de cocina internacional (categoría: Side). Importada de TheMealDB.",
      "emoji": "🍽️",
      "image": "https://www.themealdb.com/images/media/meals/5mfmh01780158856.jpg",
      "source": "themealdb",
      "diets": [
        "vegetariano",
        "sin-lactosa"
      ],
      "cuisine": "internacional",
      "suitableFor": [
        "desayuno",
        "almuerzo"
      ],
      "prepMinutes": 15,
      "cookMinutes": 30,
      "servings": 4,
      "ingredients": [
        {
          "name": "Yeast",
          "quantity": 1,
          "unit": "Tsp",
          "category": "otros"
        },
        {
          "name": "Warm water",
          "quantity": 0.5,
          "unit": "cups",
          "category": "despensa"
        },
        {
          "name": "Salt",
          "quantity": 1,
          "unit": "tsp",
          "category": "condimentos"
        },
        {
          "name": "Flour",
          "quantity": 3,
          "unit": "Cups",
          "category": "granos"
        },
        {
          "name": "Egg yolks",
          "quantity": 1,
          "unit": "For brushing",
          "category": "proteinas"
        },
        {
          "name": "Poppy seeds",
          "quantity": 1,
          "unit": "tsp",
          "category": "otros"
        }
      ],
      "steps": [
        {
          "text": "First a quick note about tandoori bread (or tandoori anything, really)"
        },
        {
          "text": "The name comes from the clay oven, or \"tandoor\" that it is traditionally cooked in, and you will never be able to duplicate the flavor of any tandoori recipe without one of those ovens, no matter how hard you try"
        },
        {
          "text": "Now, a tandoor oven is actually a part of my dream kitchen (I love naan bread and tandoori chicken) but I don't have one in my current kitchen, so this bread just goes in a plain oven, which makes it not very authentic"
        },
        {
          "text": "However, this is how an Azerbaijani stranded in the US would make a tandoori bread, so I guess I don't feel too bad about including it in my meal"
        },
        {
          "text": "The ingredients for this bread are roughly similar to the ingredients for a basic french bread, but the shape is different and it is topped with poppy seeds which actually makes it quite beautiful in appearance"
        },
        {
          "text": "In fact this bread is quite possibly the most beautiful thing I've ever baked (my cakes certainly don't fall into that category)"
        },
        {
          "text": "So as always I used my bread machine, but this time I didn't proof the yeast first"
        },
        {
          "text": "I just put it in the little yeast dispenser at the top of my machine, then added the water, flour and salt to the bucket"
        },
        {
          "text": "I put it on the dough cycle and then went and picked my kids up from school"
        },
        {
          "text": "This bread uses very basic ingredients, including bread flour and salt"
        },
        {
          "text": "If you want to do it the old-fashioned way:"
        },
        {
          "text": "Mix the yeast with the water and let stand for a few minutes"
        },
        {
          "text": "Then sift the flour with the salt into a large bowl"
        },
        {
          "text": "Gradually add the water and yeast and mix with your hand until the dough forms a ball"
        },
        {
          "text": "Turn out onto a lightly floured surface"
        },
        {
          "text": "Knead the dough for 8 to 10 minutes, or until it is smooth"
        },
        {
          "text": "Put it in a large bowl and cover, then let it rise in a warm spot until doubled (this typically takes 1 to 1 1/2 hours)"
        },
        {
          "text": "The dough after it has risen"
        },
        {
          "text": "Punch down and turn out onto a lightly floured surface"
        },
        {
          "text": "Stretch the dough until it is an oblong shape, then with a rolling pin roll it until it is about 1/2 inch thick"
        },
        {
          "text": "Transfer to a greased or non-stick baking sheet and let stand for another 15 minutes"
        },
        {
          "text": "After stretching and rolling, your dough should be roughly this shape"
        },
        {
          "text": "Cut crosshatches in the top of the dough, about four in either direction"
        },
        {
          "text": "Brush with the beaten egg yolk (I mixed mine with a little bit of water to make it easier to work with) and sprinkle with poppy seeds"
        },
        {
          "text": "Crosshatches, egg wash and poppy seeds give this bread its distinctive look"
        },
        {
          "text": "Bake in a preheated oven at about 400 degrees for 20 to 25 minutes, until golden on top"
        }
      ],
      "tips": [],
      "nutrition": {
        "kcal": 0,
        "protein": 0,
        "carbs": 0,
        "fat": 0
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "tmdb-52975",
      "title": "Tuna and Egg Briks",
      "description": "Receta de Tunisian (categoría: Seafood). Importada de TheMealDB.",
      "emoji": "🍽️",
      "image": "https://www.themealdb.com/images/media/meals/2dsltq1560461468.jpg",
      "source": "themealdb",
      "diets": [
        "sin-lactosa"
      ],
      "cuisine": "tunisian",
      "suitableFor": [
        "desayuno",
        "almuerzo"
      ],
      "prepMinutes": 15,
      "cookMinutes": 30,
      "servings": 4,
      "ingredients": [
        {
          "name": "Olive oil",
          "quantity": 2,
          "unit": "tbs",
          "category": "despensa"
        },
        {
          "name": "Spring onions",
          "quantity": 8,
          "unit": "unidades",
          "category": "verduras"
        },
        {
          "name": "Spinach",
          "quantity": 200,
          "unit": "g",
          "category": "verduras"
        },
        {
          "name": "Filo pastry",
          "quantity": 4,
          "unit": "unidades",
          "category": "otros"
        },
        {
          "name": "Tuna",
          "quantity": 1,
          "unit": "can",
          "category": "proteinas"
        },
        {
          "name": "Eggs",
          "quantity": 2,
          "unit": "unidades",
          "category": "proteinas"
        },
        {
          "name": "Hotsauce",
          "quantity": 1,
          "unit": "Dash",
          "category": "otros"
        },
        {
          "name": "Tomatoes",
          "quantity": 4,
          "unit": "Chopped",
          "category": "verduras"
        },
        {
          "name": "Cucumber",
          "quantity": 0.25,
          "unit": "unidades",
          "category": "otros"
        },
        {
          "name": "Lemon juice",
          "quantity": 1,
          "unit": "tbs",
          "category": "frutas"
        },
        {
          "name": "Apricot jam",
          "quantity": 4,
          "unit": "tbs",
          "category": "otros"
        }
      ],
      "steps": [
        {
          "text": "Heat 2 tsp of the oil in a large saucepan and cook the spring onions over a low heat for 3 minutes or until beginning to soften"
        },
        {
          "text": "Add the spinach, cover with a tight-fitting lid and cook for a further 2–3 minutes or until tender and wilted, stirring once or twice"
        },
        {
          "text": "Tip the mixture into a sieve or colander and leave to drain and cool"
        },
        {
          "text": "Using a saucer as a guide, cut out 24 rounds about 12.5 cm (5 in) in diameter from the filo pastry, cutting 6 rounds from each sheet"
        },
        {
          "text": "Stack the filo rounds in a pile, then cover with cling film to prevent them from drying out"
        },
        {
          "text": "When the spinach mixture is cool, squeeze out as much excess liquid as possible, then transfer to a bowl"
        },
        {
          "text": "Add the tuna, eggs, hot pepper sauce, and salt and pepper to taste"
        },
        {
          "text": "Mix well"
        },
        {
          "text": "Preheat the oven to 200°C (400°F, gas mark 6)"
        },
        {
          "text": "Take one filo round and very lightly brush with some of the remaining oil"
        },
        {
          "text": "Top with a second round and brush with a little oil, then place a third round on top and brush with oil"
        },
        {
          "text": "Place a heaped tbsp of the filling in the middle of the round, then fold the pastry over to make a half-moon shape"
        },
        {
          "text": "Fold in the edges, twisting them to seal, and place on a non-stick baking sheet"
        },
        {
          "text": "Repeat with the remaining pastry and filling to make 8 briks in all"
        },
        {
          "text": "Lightly brush the briks with the remaining oil"
        },
        {
          "text": "Bake for 12–15 minutes or until the pastry is crisp and golden brown"
        },
        {
          "text": "Meanwhile, combine the tomatoes and cucumber in a bowl and sprinkle with the lemon juice and seasoning to taste"
        },
        {
          "text": "Serve the briks hot with this salad and the chutney."
        }
      ],
      "tips": [],
      "nutrition": {
        "kcal": 0,
        "protein": 0,
        "carbs": 0,
        "fat": 0
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "tmdb-53561",
      "title": "Codfish deviled eggs",
      "description": "Receta de cocina internacional (categoría: Seafood). Importada de TheMealDB.",
      "emoji": "🍽️",
